title: moon4_bronze_intro
---
Milo: The Bronze Moon. The Star Fort awaits.
Milo: This is a different kind of architecture. Defensive. Built when the giants knew the Mud Flood was coming.
Milo: They were trying to save themselves.
===

title: moon4_korath_first_meeting
---
Korath: *(massive voice, deep — somewhere between earthquake and lullaby)*
Korath: TRAVELER. You are the first small one to walk these halls in seven hundred years.
Korath: I am Korath. Architect-Singer. Fourth of seven.
Korath: My brother sleeps inside that golem you fight. My other brother... is the dissonance you hear.
===

title: moon4_korath_explains_brothers
---
Korath: Three brothers. Three songs.
Korath: Maelix sang the harmonic. I sing the structure.
Korath: Zereth — *(pause)* — Zereth sang transcendence. He sang too loud. He cracked. The Parasite Cabal heard him crack, and they hijacked him.
Korath: The Dissonant One. He is my brother, and he is the weapon they made of my brother.
===

title: moon4_korath_combat_companion
---
Korath: *(laughing as he lifts a boulder)*
Korath: STONE DOES NOT FORGET ITS SONG.
Korath: Watch — when I sing this fortress's note, the golems shatter.
Korath: We will sing the siege apart together, traveler. You with your small precise notes, me with my big thundering one.
===

title: moon4_korath_sacrifice
---
Korath: I will pour the rest of myself into this bell tower.
Korath: When I am done, half the planetary grid will sing for one transcendent moment.
Korath: The sky itself will hear. The other Moons will know we are still here.
Korath: *(softer)* And you will know what a giant sounds like, the moment before he becomes light.
===

title: moon4_korath_farewell
---
Korath: Carry the song forward, small one. You have it in you now.
Korath: When you reach the Twelfth Moon — when you ring the Mirror Bell — listen for my echo.
Korath: I will be inside the bell, waiting.
===
